# Agentforce Lightning Types (Cursor Rule)

Apex-based CLTs for Agentforce chat surfaces. Follow the **JSON-string envelope**. The legacy `sourceType`/`lightning__listType` binding breaks renderer registration; don't use it.

**Generate** a new card with `sf-clt-builder` (surface adapter, templates, GenAiFunction flags). **Debug** a card that will not render with `agentforce-lightning-types` (ECv2 Connection, ESD republish, ShowCommand). Cowork write-back is unverified — display-only / `NavigationMixin`.

## When to apply
- "Lightning Type", "CLT", "agent chat UI", "Agentforce render", "custom output rendering".
- Files in `lightningTypes/**`, or an LWC `js-meta.xml` with `lightning__AgentforceInput`/`lightning__AgentforceOutput`.

## When NOT to apply
- Object-based CLTs for Experience Builder / Prompt Builder / Mosaic.
- MIAW (non–Chat V2). Plain LWCs on record/app/home pages.

## Dual naming
- **Apex DTO class** (`SummitRidgeEquipmentOutput`) ← LT `schema.json` `@apexClassType/c__<Class>`
- **LT folder** (`summitRidgeEquipmentOutput`) ← GenAi output `lightning:type` `c__<folder>`
- **LWC** (`summitRidgeEquipmentCard`) ← `renderer.json` `c/<lwc>`
- **JSON field** (`equipmentJSON`) ← LWC `this.value.equipmentJSON`

## File structure
```
lightningTypes/<Type>/
  <Type>.lightningType-meta.xml   # working deploys; some docs say lightningTypeBundle-meta.xml
  schema.json
  lightningDesktopGenAi/
    renderer.json                 # ONLY this folder. Do NOT add enhancedWebChat/.
    editor.json                   # only if collecting input
```
New LWCs: apiVersion **67.0**. Bundle floor 64.0+. Agentforce targets 62.0+.

## Envelope
Renderer DTO: `global`, `@JsonAccess(serializable='always' deserializable='always')`, ONE `@AuraEnabled String`. Two constructors. Never share across renderers.

```apex
@JsonAccess(serializable='always' deserializable='always')
global class Acme_AccountHealthData {
    @AuraEnabled global String healthJSON;
    global Acme_AccountHealthData(String j) { this.healthJSON = j; }
    global Acme_AccountHealthData() { this.healthJSON = ''; }
}
```

Action `Response` fields use `@InvocableVariable`. Displayable field is typed as the **DTO class**, always populated (sentinel `{"error":"..."}` on failure). Pair with 2–3 planner passthrough scalars.

**Display flags (two independent flags):** card `isDisplayable: true` / `isUsedByPlanner: false` (Path B: `is_displayable: True` / `filter_from_agent: True`). Passthroughs inverse. `is_displayable` gates the render tool; filtering hides JSON so the planner does not narrate it.

`schema.json`: `"lightning:type": "@apexClassType/c__<DtoClass>"`. Use `c__` at creation.

`renderer.json`:
```json
{ "renderer": { "componentOverrides": { "$": { "definition": "c/acmeAccountHealth" } } } }
```
`lightningDesktopGenAi/` ONLY. No `attributes`. No `enhancedWebChat/` — the compatibility table lists it as valid, but adding it has broken working desktop configs. ECv2 falls back to desktop when it is missing (privacy: a rep card can reach a customer).

## LWC
Targets only `lightning__AgentforceOutput`(+`Input`). No `sourceType`/`targetConfigs`/`lightningSnapin__ChatMessage`. Simple `@api value`; parse in `connectedCallback` with `typeof raw === 'string' ? JSON.parse(raw) : raw`. Design at ~380px.

**Write-back is surface-specific** — do not default to `embeddedservice_bootstrap`:
- ECv2: `this.configuration?.util.sendTextMessage(...)`
- SRA: `copytochat` / `acc:execute`; Messaging send via `conversationToolkitApi` (`!== false`)
- Employee LEX: `lightning/accApi` `execute()`
- Cowork: none verified

## ShowCommand vs InformCommand
The planner decides whether the LWC mounts. Vague instructions → InformCommand (`result: []`). Put `show_command` language on the action description + LT `schema.json` description; keep topic instructions minimal. Diagnose: Network → `messages/stream` → `result: []`. Switch console context to the Agentforce Messaging **iframe**.

## Deploy / permset / test
Path A: DTO → (LT+LWC) → GenAiFunction → permset → **deactivate agent** → planner → reactivate.
Path B: DTO → service → (LT+LWC) → permset → `sf agent validate` → publish → activate.
- EinsteinServiceAgent → permset on `<botUser>` (`--on-behalf-of`). Employee/Cowork → logged-in users.
- Builder preview **can** render CLTs as of 262 (AEA always; ASA when connected to ECv2). Always confirm on the real surface. Republish the ESD after every change.

